{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Itinerary for a Noble Traveller in the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\n**Act the First: The Arrival in the Imperial City of Tokyo**\n\nUpon the morrow thou shalt set foot in the fair city of Edo now known as Tokyo where the neon lights do dance like fairies in the night. First visit the grand Shinto shrine of Meiji where thou mayest seek the blessings of the kami the spirits of nature. Then proceed to the bustling marketplace of Takeshita Street in Harajuku where the youth do gather in their finery and the wares are as diverse as the stars in heaven.\n\nNext thou shalt venture to the towering edifice of Tokyo Skytree where the city doth sprawl beneath thee like a tapestry woven by the gods. When the sun doth wane dine at a traditional izakaya in Shinjuku where the sake flows like the river of life and the morsels are a feast for the senses.\n\n**Act the Second: The Pilgrimage to the Ancient Capital of Kyoto**\n\nTake the swift Shinkansen to the ancient city of Kyoto where the past doth whisper on the wind. First visit the famed Kinkaku-ji the Golden Pavilion where the roof doth gleam like burnished gold and the reflections in the pond are as true as the heavens above.\n\nThen journey to the sacred grounds of Fushimi Inari where thousands of vermilion torii gates do form a path to the mountain’s peak a sight most wondrous and humbling. In the evening attend a traditional tea ceremony where the matcha is prepared with grace and the sweets are as delicate as the blossoms of spring.\n\n**Act the Third: The Sojourn to the Sacred Isle of Miyajima**\n\nFrom Kyoto thou shalt journey to the isle of Miyajima where the torii gate of Itsukushima doth stand as though floating upon the sea at high tide. Walk the paths of the island and marvel at the deer who roam as though they own the land and the maple trees that turn to flame in the autumn.\n\nStay in a ryokan where the tatami mats are soft beneath thy feet and the kaiseki meal is a symphony of flavors. As the sun doth set take a boat upon the waters to view the gate bathed in the glow of the moon a sight most ethereal and grand.\n\n**Act the Fourth: The Retreat to the Land of the Northern Lights**\n\nTravel to the northern isle of Hokkaido where the air is crisp and the landscapes are as vast as the sea. In Sapporo visit the Clock Tower and the grand Odori Park where the snow festivals do weave their magic in winter.\n\nVenture to the wilderness of Daisetsuzan National Park where the mountains do touch the heavens and the hot springs do soothe the soul. Feast upon the local delicacies such as the savory soup of miso ramen and the sweet delights of butter-filled soft serve ice cream.\n\n**Act the Fifth: The Farewell to the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\nAs thy journey doth draw to a close return to Tokyo to procure souvenirs and gifts for thy kin. Visit the serene Shinjuku Gyoen where the gardens are a symphony of color and tranquility.\n\nOn thy final eve attend a traditional kabuki performance where the actors do bring ancient tales to life with grace and skill. Raise a final cup of sake to the gods of travel and bid adieu to this land of wonders.\n\nThus concludes thy grand adventure in the Land of the Rising Sun. May thy journey be filled with marvels and thy heart be light as thou dost traverse this realm of beauty and mystery. Fare thee well noble traveller and may thy travels be ever in thy favor.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.40493902564048767}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.06451141834259033}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.7151038646697998}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.5446437001228333}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -4.172316494077677e-06}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -5.722029527532868e-06}, {"token": " It", "logprob": -0.21236224472522736}, {"token": "iner", "logprob": -0.00025674383505247533}, {"token": "ary", "logprob": -